    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d824">

                <pb facs="0769" n="757" xml:id="pg757"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R./1019: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-04-29T19:00:00-03:00">April 29, 1940—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 29—5:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>183. Department’s No. 114, April 27, 2 p.m. Aranha says that he is in accord with
                    the Department’s attitude to the Argentine proposal and if President Vargas
                    agrees (he is sure he will agree) he will adopt a corresponding attitude in the
                    premises.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
